exercises.solution:
- 8 booleanity constraints $x_i \cdot x_i = x_i$;
- 1 decomposition constraint $(x_0 + 2x_1 + \cdots + 128x_7) \cdot 1 = x$;
- $x \cdot x = t$ (a new variable $t = x^2$);
- $t \cdot x = y - x$: the right-hand side is a linear combination, so the addition is free.

Total: $8 + 1 + 1 + 1 = \mathbf{11}$. Since $x < 256$, $x^3 + x < 2^{25}$, which is smaller than the field size of any real SNARK, so the field equation is the integer equation. Writing $t \cdot x = u$ and then $(u + x) \cdot 1 = y$ also works but wastes a constraint; minimising multiplications is the everyday craft of circuit writing.

